      "snippet": {
        "text": "Assessment and learning are two interrelated things (Brown, 2005). \n\nAssessment has an important role to create the 21 st century generation. The 21 stcentury generation is expected to own special skills as to adapt to the digital era. \n\nAccording to the International Society for Technology in Education (2007)  due to the occurrence of digital skills, but one thing that will not change is the skill itself. In order to prepare the 21st century generation, it is necessary to revitalize the assessment strategy. The assessment required is an assessment that can provide constructive feedback and serves as a learning tool. The assessment of such characteristics is necessary to prepare students to be lifelong learners and to be reflective. This explanation aims to (1) describe the pattern of feedback in the writing assessments in junior high school (2) describe the use of self-regulation in writing assessments, (3) analyze feedback according to the principles of feedback, and ( 4) analyze self-regulation in the assessment perspective as learning tools (assessment as learning).",
