      "snippet": {
        "text": "Formative assessment encompasses a range of techniques employed by educators to assess student understanding, identify learning requirements, and monitor academic advancement throughout a session, unit, or course. Classroom applications such as Kahoot! and Quizizz are utilized to generate enjoyable and interactive quizzes, offering prompt feedback to students (Manasia et al., 2020). These tools assist educators in pinpointing areas where pupils require supplementary assistance. Educators employ Google Forms to streamline the process of peer evaluations. Students assess one another's work, offering constructive criticism and contemplating their own learning process (Government of South Africa, 2020). This approach fosters development of analytical reasoning and ability to evaluate oneself. Teachers utilize regular feedback loops via platforms such as Padlet, which allows students to share their work and receive immediate feedback from both teachers and peers (Ramrathan, 2021). \n\nThis continuous evaluation aids in tracking student advancement and adapting instructional approaches accordingly. Regular feedback is crucial for monitoring progress and finding areas for improvement in continuous evaluation systems. Utilizing digital tools to do formative evaluations can provide instant insights into student performance. The Free State province utilizes online quizzes and assignments during lockdowns. It serves as a prime example of how technology can enable continuous evaluation and aid in tailoring learning routes to individual needs (Eleyyan, 2021).",
