      "snippet": {
        "text": "In addition, the high workload of teachers often hinders the optimal implementation of formative assessment, considering that this approach requires great effort in designing tasks, providing feedback, and monitoring student progress. Although the benefits of formative assessment have been widely recognized, its implementation in the field often encounters obstacles, especially in environments with limited resources. \n\nThe solution to overcome the problem is to try to make teachers play a crucial role in the implementation of formative assessment. They not only act as evaluators but also as facilitators who guide students in the learning process. By using formative assessment, teachers can identify gaps in students' understanding and design relevant interventions. In this case, feedback becomes a key element. Effective feedback must be specific, relevant, and actionable, so that students understand their strengths and weaknesses and can take steps to improve their learning. Formative assessment allows teachers to monitor students' progress and activeness to regulate their own learning (Babkova & Poliuga, 2023;Z. Yan et al., 2021). Formative assessment can increase students' active cognitive engagement and facilitate their understanding of learning content. Formative assessment is designed to provide information that teachers and students can use in real time to improve learning. Thus, this approach strengthens student-oriented education, where students play an active role in their learning journey. \n\nPrevious research findings showed that there was an influence between formative assessment using Quizizz media on the learning outcomes of grade VI elementary school students (Halimah et al., 2023). Greater perceived use of formative assessment is associated with higher feelings of competence, and better motivation (Leenknecht et al., 2021). Formative electronic assessments help students monitor progress and encourage further study and enhance learning and understanding (McCallum & Milner, 2021). However, most studies still focus on the direct relationship between formative assessment and academic achievement, while in-depth studies on its application in specific contexts, such as online learning or metacognitive skills, are still limited. This study aims to analyze the effectiveness of formative assessment as an approach to improve student learning outcomes at various levels of education.",
