udies in Hattie's meta-synthesis (2016) revealed a moderate effect of formative evaluation on student learning (d = .68).\n\nSimilar to self-monitoring and self-assessment, formative assessment aims to provide learners with feedback about their progress. However, in formative assessment the teacher monitors the students' learning and provides them with external feedback, whereas in self-assessment the learners have to self-",
