      "snippet": {
        "text": "The design used for the study a pre-test, post-test non randomized control group quasi experimental research design which consisted of two instructional groups. The independent variables were two different types of instructional approaches; instruction based on computer with internet connection for formative assessment following feedback, and teaching without using feedback and formative assessment while the dependent variable were students' academic achievement. In quasi-experimental research design, each group was given both a pre-test and a post-test, measuring the dependent variable before and after exposure to independent variable.",
